ADDENDA <Presidential Decree No. 35099, Dec. 24, 2024>
Article 1 (Enforcement date)
This Decree shall enter into force on the date of its promulgation; provided, the amended provisions of subparagraph 2 of Appendix 1-2 shall enter into force 1 year after the date of the promulgation.
Article 2 (Special Cases concerning building asbestos inspections for community children's centers)
(1) Notwithstanding the amended provisions of subparagraph 2 of Appendix 1-2, the owner of a community children's center under those amended provisions which is in use as of the enforcement date under the proviso of Article 1 of the Addenda, with a total floor area of less than 500 square meters, shall require an asbestos inspection institution to conduct a building asbestos inspection pursuant to Article 21(1) of the Act, deeming the enforcement date under the proviso of Article 1 of the Addenda as the date of receiving approval for use under Article 22(2) of the Building Act.
(2) Notwithstanding paragraph (1), if an asbestos inspection has been conducted on a building before the enforcement date under the proviso of Article 1 of the Addenda, and the Minister of Environment recognizes the inspection as adequate, as prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Environment, a building asbestos inspection under Article 21(1) of the Act shall be deemed to have been conducted.
(3) The owner of a building recognized as adequate by the Minister of Environment pursuant to paragraph (2) shall submit the materials prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Environment to the competent Special Self-Governing City Mayor or Special Self-Governing Province Governor, or the head of the relevant Si/Gun/Gu, within 1 month from the date of receiving the notification of recognition.

